* REF3012 behavioural model written for this project (not the vendor model).
* Datasheet numbers it uses (TI REF3012): 1.25 V output, 1.8 V minimum supply,
* 42 uA typical supply current. The output starts regulating as IN rises
* through about 1.3 V to 1.6 V and is flat above that.
* Assumed: 0.5 ohm output resistance. Not modelled: noise, line and load
* regulation, temperature drift, turn-on settling time.
* The +/-0.2 % initial accuracy is handled as a corner parameter (err).
* Pins: IN OUT GND
.subckt REF3012 in out gnd params: err=0
Iq in gnd DC 42u
Bref oi gnd V = 1.25*(1+{err})/(1+exp(-(V(in,gnd)-1.45)/0.03))
Rout oi out 0.5
.ends REF3012
